      { id: 'django', name: 'Server-rendered and scoped in the view', code:
`<!-- portal/templates/portal/orders.html. It extends portal/base.html and not
     the console's base.html, because the console base renders app-shell — the
     sidebar, the counts, the palette, the internal nav — and a portal page that
     inherits it hands a supplier the shape of our whole application and a
     column of numbers they may not see. Two bases, and the portal one is small.

     The scoping is the security boundary and it belongs in the view. Every
     queryset in the portal is filtered to request.user.supplier_contact.vendor
     before anything else touches it, and no template in this directory is
     allowed to widen it: a template condition is a display rule that somebody
     will move when the layout changes, and the day it moves the page is still
     valid HTML and still renders. Write it once, in a mixin, and make the
     detail view raise Http404 rather than PermissionDenied — a 403 on somebody
     else's order and a 404 on an order that does not exist is an enumeration
     oracle, and outside the company that is a leak of who we buy from.

     {% csrf_token %} sits in the sign-out form because sign-out is a POST.
     Django's LogoutView has refused GET since 4.1, and a GET sign-out is fired
     by link prefetchers and by the mail scanners that follow every URL in a
     notification — the supplier is then signed out by an email nobody opened.

     |intcomma is what puts ₹21,31,200 in Indian grouping, and it raises without
     {% load humanize %} in this same file. That is why the load line is here
     rather than only in the base.

     The empty clause is a real state on this page and it is not "no results" — there
     is no query to clear. A supplier with nothing open needs to be told that
     the portal is working and that new orders arrive here, or the empty screen
     reads as a broken account.

     A multi-line {# #} is not a comment: Django's tag_re has no DOTALL, so
     everything after the first line renders on the page. The view notes at the
     foot are in a comment/endcomment block for exactly that reason. -->
{% extends "portal/base.html" %}
{% load humanize %}

{% block main %}
<div data-kui="portal-page/django" class="min-h-[560px] bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-900">

  <header class="border-b border-zinc-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-5xl flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 px-4 py-2.5">
      <a href="{% url 'portal:home' %}" class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2.5 rounded-lg focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-700 text-[13px]/5 font-semibold text-white">K</span>
        <span class="min-w-0">
          <span class="block truncate text-[13px]/5 font-semibold">Konspec Industries</span>
          <span class="block truncate text-[11px]/4 text-zinc-500">Supplier portal</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <div class="ml-auto flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2.5">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-200 text-[12px]/4 font-medium text-zinc-600 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-300">{{ vendor.initials }}</span>
        <span class="min-w-0">
          <span class="block truncate text-[13px]/5 font-medium">{{ vendor.name }}</span>
          <span class="block truncate text-[11px]/4 text-zinc-500">{{ request.user.get_full_name }}</span>
        </span>
        <form method="post" action="{% url 'portal:logout' %}" class="shrink-0">
          {% csrf_token %}
          <button type="submit" class="rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 text-[13px]/5 font-medium text-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-200 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">Sign out</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>

    <nav aria-label="Supplier portal" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-2 pb-2">
      <ul class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1">
        <li><a href="{% url 'portal:orders' %}" aria-current="page" class="block rounded-lg bg-zinc-200 px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 font-medium text-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-300 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">Orders</a></li>
        <li><a href="{% url 'portal:invoices' %}" class="block rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600 hover:bg-zinc-100 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">Invoices</a></li>
        <li><a href="{% url 'portal:payments' %}" class="block rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600 hover:bg-zinc-100 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">Payments</a></li>
        <li><a href="{% url 'portal:details' %}" class="block rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600 hover:bg-zinc-100 hover:text-zinc-900 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">Your details</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-5">
    <h1 class="text-[24px]/7 font-semibold tracking-tight">Your orders</h1>
    <p class="mt-1.5 max-w-2xl text-[14px]/5 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">
      All {{ orders|length|intcomma }} orders Konspec Industries has open with {{ vendor.name }}. There is nothing else on this portal to find — if an order you expect is missing, it has not been raised yet.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-zinc-300 bg-white">
      <table class="hidden w-full text-[13px]/5 md:table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Purchase orders placed by Konspec Industries with {{ vendor.name }}</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 text-left text-[11px]/4 font-medium tracking-wider text-zinc-600 uppercase">
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">Konspec order</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">Your reference</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 text-right font-medium">Value</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 text-right font-medium">Wanted by</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium">What we are waiting for</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for o in orders %}
            <tr class="border-b border-zinc-100 align-top last:border-0 hover:bg-zinc-100">
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                <span class="block font-medium tabular-nums">{{ o.number }}</span>
                <span class="mt-0.5 block text-[12px]/4 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">{{ o.material }} · {{ o.quantity }} {{ o.unit }}</span>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">{{ o.vendor_reference|default:"—" }}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">₹{{ o.value|intcomma }}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap text-zinc-600">{{ o.wanted_by|date:"d M Y" }}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                {% comment %}
                  status_dot_class comes off the model and is one of the five
                  locked values — bg-zinc-500, bg-amber-500, bg-red-600,
                  bg-emerald-600, bg-zinc-400 — so the pill shape is written
                  once here and only the dot changes. supplier_status is the
                  word a supplier reads; get_status_display is the internal one
                  and never reaches this template.
                {% endcomment %}
                <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-zinc-200 px-2 py-0.5 text-[12px]/4 text-zinc-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-300">
                  <span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full {{ o.status_dot_class }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ o.supplier_status }}
                </span>
                {% if o.needs_acknowledgement %}
                  <a href="{% url 'portal:acknowledge' o.number %}"
                     class="mt-2 block w-fit rounded-lg border border-transparent bg-zinc-700 px-3 py-1.5 text-[13px]/5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-800 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/30">
                    Accept or change the date
                  </a>
                {% elif o.awaiting_invoice %}
                  <a href="{% url 'portal:invoice-new' %}?receipt={{ o.receipt.number }}"
                     class="mt-2 block w-fit rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-[13px]/5 font-medium hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">
                    Send your invoice
                  </a>
                {% else %}
                  <span class="mt-1.5 block text-[12px]/4 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">{{ o.supplier_next_step }}</span>
                {% endif %}
              </td>
            </tr>
          {% empty %}
            <tr>
              <td colspan="5" class="px-6 py-12 text-center">
                <span class="mx-auto flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-zinc-200 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-300">
                  <i data-lucide="package" class="size-5 text-zinc-600"></i>
                </span>
                <h2 class="mt-3 text-[16px]/6 font-semibold">Konspec has no open orders with you</h2>
                <p class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-sm text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600">
                  Nothing is outstanding between us at the moment. A new order appears here the same day it is raised, and {{ request.user.email }} is emailed when it does.
                </p>
                <a href="{% url 'portal:payments' %}"
                   class="mt-4 inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-white px-4 text-[13px]/5 font-medium hover:bg-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">
                  See your payments
                </a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <ul class="divide-y divide-zinc-100 md:hidden">
        {% for o in orders %}
          <li class="px-4 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <span class="text-[14px]/5 font-medium tabular-nums">{{ o.number }}</span>
              <span class="shrink-0 text-[14px]/5 tabular-nums">₹{{ o.value|intcomma }}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-[13px]/5 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">{{ o.material }} · {{ o.quantity }} {{ o.unit }}</p>
            <p class="mt-0.5 text-[12px]/4 tabular-nums text-zinc-500">Your reference {{ o.vendor_reference|default:"—" }} · wanted by {{ o.wanted_by|date:"d M Y" }}</p>
            <span class="mt-2 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-zinc-200 px-2 py-0.5 text-[12px]/4 text-zinc-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-zinc-300">
              <span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full {{ o.status_dot_class }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ o.supplier_status }}
            </span>
            {% if o.needs_acknowledgement %}
              <a href="{% url 'portal:acknowledge' o.number %}"
                 class="mt-3 flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-transparent bg-zinc-700 px-4 text-[13px]/5 font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-800 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/30">
                Accept or change the date
              </a>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
        {% empty %}
          <li class="px-6 py-10 text-center">
            <h2 class="text-[16px]/6 font-semibold">Konspec has no open orders with you</h2>
            <p class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-sm text-[13px]/5 text-zinc-600">A new order appears here the same day it is raised.</p>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pb-6">
    <p class="border-t border-zinc-200 pt-4 text-[12px]/4 tabular-nums text-zinc-600">
      Your buyer at Konspec is <span class="font-medium text-zinc-900">{{ vendor.buyer.get_full_name }}</span> —
      <a href="mailto:{{ vendor.buyer.email }}" class="font-medium text-zinc-900 underline underline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-zinc-700/15">{{ vendor.buyer.email }}</a>
      · {{ vendor.buyer.phone }}. Anything this portal cannot do, she can.
    </p>
  </footer>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% comment %}
portal/views.py — the scoping, written once and never in a template

    class VendorScopedMixin(LoginRequiredMixin):
        """The security boundary of the whole portal.

        Every queryset starts here. Nothing in portal/templates may widen it:
        a template condition is a display rule and somebody will move it, and
        the page still renders perfectly the day they do.
        """
        def get_vendor(self):
            return self.request.user.supplier_contact.vendor

        def get_queryset(self):
            return super().get_queryset().filter(vendor=self.get_vendor())

    class OrderList(VendorScopedMixin, ListView):
        model = PurchaseOrder
        context_object_name = 'orders'
        template_name = 'portal/orders.html'

        def get_queryset(self):
            return (super().get_queryset()
                    .exclude(status=PurchaseOrder.DRAFT)
                    .select_related('receipt')
                    .order_by('-raised_on'))

        def get_context_data(self, **kw):
            return super().get_context_data(vendor=self.get_vendor(), **kw)

    class OrderDetail(VendorScopedMixin, DetailView):
        model = PurchaseOrder
        # 404 and not 403. A 403 on another supplier's order and a 404 on an
        # order that was never raised is an enumeration oracle: outside the
        # company it leaks who we buy from and how much we buy. get_object()
        # on the scoped queryset raises Http404 for both, which is the
        # restricted variant of this entry.

A draft order is excluded here as well as scoped. Draft is our word for an
order that has not been signed off internally, and a supplier who is emailed
about one and then finds it withdrawn has been told something that was not a
commitment.

supplier_status and supplier_next_step are model properties, not template
logic. The internal get_status_display() never reaches these templates: it says
Approved, which does not tell a supplier who approved what or what they now
owe us.
{% endcomment %}` }
